Provenance of the high-level BIOS (runtime/guests/gba/bios)

No code, table or byte of the console's BIOS image is used. Behaviour comes
from three sources, listed per function below:

  [G] GBATEK, the public hardware documentation: call numbers,
      argument and data formats.
  [C] The Cult-of-GBA replacement BIOS, https://github.com/Cult-of-GBA/BIOS,
      commit a30e9a96df083628b650724b7d4d7112b4070b98, MIT license (text
      below). Tables were adapted from it; no code was copied, the routines
      here are new C.
  [P] The SWI probe ROM's records of the console's BIOS (results, written
      memory, stack frames and cycle counts of about 3,500 calls), from which
      the side registers (r1, r3), the stack frames, the edge cases and the
      cycle cost fits were derived.

swi.c
  dispatcher frames (SPSR, r11, r12, LR on the supervisor stack; r2 and LR on
  the system stack), r2 and r12 restored                          [P]
  IRQ stub at 0x18 (r0-r3, r12, LR pushed; LR = 0x138)             [G][P]
  open-bus values after boot, IRQ and SWI                          [G]
  GetBiosChecksum, SoftReset, Halt, Stop, CustomHalt, MultiBoot    [G][P]
  post-boot state and I/O                                          [G]
  cycle cost fits per call                                         [P]
math.c
  Div, DivArm (quotient loop, signs, r3 = |quotient|, division by
  zero behaviour)                                                  [G][P]
  Sqrt (r1, r3 of the last Newton step)                            [P]
  ArcTan polynomial constants                                      [G][C]
  ArcTan2 octants and r3                                           [G][P]
  sine table (BgAffineSet, ObjAffineSet)                           [C]
  BgAffineSet, ObjAffineSet                                        [G][P]
copy.c
  CpuSet, CpuFastSet, the source check on address bits 25-27,
  the registers they leave                                         [G][P]
decomp.c
  BitUnPack, LZ77UnComp (WRAM and VRAM), HuffUnComp, RLUnComp
  (WRAM and VRAM), Diff8bitUnFilter (WRAM and VRAM),
  Diff16bitUnFilter: formats                                      [G]
  r0, r1, r3 left, VRAM odd-byte handling, stack contents          [P]
misc.c
  RegisterRamReset areas and order                                 [G][C][P]
  IntrWait, VBlankIntrWait                                         [G][P]
  SoundBias                                                        [G]
  MidiKey2Freq scale and frequency tables                          [C]
  MidiKey2Freq arithmetic                                          [G][P]

Not used: Normmatt/gba_bios (a disassembly of the console's BIOS without a
license), and every GPL-licensed emulator.

